title: Tactics units
intro: Pick a unit, see how far it can walk and hit, then send it in. Two sides take turns, with no code.
project: Empty | Skirmish

chapter: Four units on a field | Entity > Genres > Tactics > Tactics Unit
create: Tilemap
rename: Field
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 1111111111\n1........1\n1...11...1\n1........1\n1........1\n1111111111
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position.X = 5
set: Transform.Position.Y = -3
look: 5, -3, 4
deselect
create: Tactics Unit
rename: Knight
set: Transform.Position = 1.5, -2.5, 0
explain: component:TacticsUnit | Tactics Unit | Tactics Unit, under Tactics, makes a unit: it walks up to four cells a turn and hits whatever is next to it.
explain: panel:Hierarchy | Turns and controls | The first unit also brings a turn order, Blue then Red, with an End Turn button, and the tactics controls that let you pick units with the mouse.
create: Tactics Unit
rename: Orc
set: Transform.Position = 8.5, -2.5, 0
say: The next unit goes on the Red side, so making units one after another makes two even teams.
create: Tactics Unit
rename: Archer
set: Transform.Position = 1.5, -3.5, 0
set: TacticsUnit.Move = 3
set: TacticsUnit.Range = 3
set: TacticsUnit.MinRange = 2
explain: field:TacticsUnit.Range | Range and Min Range | An archer shoots two or three cells away, but can't hit what's right next to it.
create: Tactics Unit
rename: Goblin
set: Transform.Position = 8.5, -3.5, 0
say: And a goblin for Red.
select: Turns
set: TurnOrder.ComputerSides =
explain: field:TurnOrder.ComputerSides | Computer Sides | The computer plays Red to begin with. Clearing Computer Sides makes it two people taking turns at one keyboard.

chapter: Blue's turn | Pick, look, walk
play
wait: 0.5
gameclick: Knight
wait: 0.3
explain: game | Where it can go | Clicking the knight lights up the cells it can walk to in blue, around the wall, and the cells it could hit from them in red.
gamehover: 4.5, -1.5
wait: 0.3
explain: game | The way there | Hovering a cell shows the way it would walk.
gameclick: 4.5, -1.5
wait: 1
expectat: Knight = 4.5, -1.5
say: There's nothing in reach from there, so its go is over, and it's dimmed until Blue's next turn.
gameclick: Archer
gameclick: 3.5, -4.5
wait: 1
expectat: Archer = 3.5, -4.5
expectvalue: Turns.TurnOrder.Current = Red
say: Once every Blue unit has had its go, the turn passes to Red.

chapter: Red's turn | Take back, attack, wait
gameclick: Orc
gameclick: 5.5, -1.5
wait: 1
expectat: Orc = 5.5, -1.5
explain: game | Waiting to attack | The orc walks up next to the knight. With a foe in reach, it waits to be told whom to hit.
gameorder: 5.5, -1.5
wait: 0.4
expectat: Orc = 8.5, -2.5
say: A right click takes the walk back, as long as it hasn't attacked yet.
gameclick: Knight
wait: 1.2
expectvalue: Knight.Health.Current = 2
explain: game | Click a foe | Clicking a foe straight away walks up to it and attacks. The knight's health bar drops.
gameclick: Goblin
gameclick: Goblin
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Turns.TurnOrder.Current = Blue
say: Clicking a unit twice has it wait where it stands, and it's Blue's turn again.

chapter: Blue strikes back | Range
gameclick: Archer
gameclick: Orc
wait: 1.2
expectvalue: Orc.Health.Current = 2
explain: game | From a distance | The archer walks to where the orc is two or three cells off, and shoots it.
gameclick: Knight
gameclick: Orc
wait: 0.6
expectvalue: Orc.Health.Current = 1
say: The knight is right next to the orc, so it hits from where it stands.
stop
say: That's tactics with no code: a Tactics Unit for each fighter, with its move, range and damage, and the controls do the rest.
